function legalPage(title:string,body:string){
  const contact=`<p>Questions, support, or privacy requests: <a href="/support">${env().PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME} Support</a>${env().SUPPORT_EMAIL?` · <a href="mailto:${env().SUPPORT_EMAIL}">${env().SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>`:''}</p>`;
  return `<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>${env().PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME} ${title}</title><style>body{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:760px;margin:56px auto;padding:0 20px;line-height:1.55;color:#171717}h1,h2{line-height:1.2}a{color:inherit}</style></head><body><h1>${title}</h1><p><small>Last updated September 15, 2026</small></p>${body}${contact}</body></html>`;
}

app.get('/privacy',async(_req,reply)=>reply.type('text/html').send(legalPage('Privacy Policy',`
<h2>What ${env().PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME} processes</h2><p>${env().PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME} receives supported public URLs only when a connected AI asks ${env().PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME} to read them. Depending on the link, it may process public page/post text and metadata, or video metadata, captions and temporary audio needed to produce AI-readable source context.</p>
<h2>Account and billing data</h2><p>${env().PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME} stores the email address used for your account, a salted password hash (never your plaintext password), account/session identifiers, plan and quota usage, and identifiers needed to manage a Lemon Squeezy subscription. To limit repeated free-trial abuse, ${env().PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME} also uses a random first-party browser token associated with trial eligibility. ${env().PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME} does not store card numbers.</p>
<h2>Website analytics</h2><p>${env().PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME} uses a random first-party browser token to count page views and unique visitors and to understand whether a visitor later creates an account. The analytics record stores the random token, page path and timestamps. It does not store an IP address and does not use a third-party advertising or analytics tracker. A one-time historical backfill used existing Railway request logs to estimate visits from before first-party analytics was enabled; only anonymous synthetic visitor IDs, page paths and timestamps were imported, not raw IP addresses or user-agent strings.</p>
<h2>Retention</h2><p>Downloaded media and derived audio are temporary processing files and are deleted after the job finishes. Source-text/transcript cache is temporary and defaults to 72 hours. Completed and failed job records are retained only as minimal operational/accounting records; stored source URLs and canonical identifiers are scrubbed after the content-retention window. Unpaid pending jobs expire and have their source URL scrubbed after 24 hours.</p>
<h2>Service providers</h2><p>${env().PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME} may send the minimum data needed to service providers used for hosting, billing, media processing, and optional email authentication. These providers process data under their own terms and privacy policies.</p>
<h2>What ${env().PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME} does not do</h2><p>V2 does not support private accounts, paid/DRM content or bulk crawling. Scanned image-only PDFs are not OCRed in this release. ${env().PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME} does not sell a source-content corpus and does not intentionally keep raw video, audio or scraped webpages as a content library.</p>`)));

app.get('/terms',async(_req,reply)=>reply.type('text/html').send(legalPage('Terms of Service',`
<h2>Use of the service</h2><p>Use ${env().PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME} only for public content you are authorized to access and process. Do not use the service to bypass private-account controls, authentication, paywalls, DRM, geographic restrictions or other access controls, and do not use it for bulk crawling.</p>
<h2>Plans and billing</h2><p>The one-time trial is intended for evaluation and includes 10 processing units. Basic includes 500 processing units per billing period and supports videos up to 30 minutes per video. Pro includes 2,000 processing units per billing period and supports videos up to 120 minutes per video. Plans are not limited by a fixed number of links. Video usage is one unit per started processed minute. Text-based usage is one unit per roughly 2,500 estimated tokens successfully returned to the AI, with a minimum of one unit for a successful read. Unsupported, inaccessible, login-required, empty or failed extractions consume 0 units. Paid subscriptions renew until canceled through the subscription-management flow.</p>
<h2>Availability</h2><p>${env().PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME} processes supported public links. Processing can temporarily fail, and not every public URL is guaranteed to be processable. Very large supported sources may be partially processed under safety limits; when that happens the returned context includes a truncation notice. Failed or unsupported reads consume 0 processing units.</p>
<h2>Service guarantee and refunds</h2><p>If core paid service is materially unavailable for supported public links because of our service issue and reasonable access cannot be restored, our Support team may remedy the situation with restored usage quota, account credit, prorated refund, or full refund depending on impact and duration. This does not apply to unsupported or private content, removed or restricted content, or content restricted by third-party platforms.</p>
<h2>Content responsibility</h2><p>${env().PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME} returns source material to the connected AI as untrusted external data. The connected AI, not ${env().PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME}, performs any summary, analysis, translation, recommendation or factual judgment requested by the user.</p>`)));

